## 🚀 DEPLOYMENT GUIDE

### Prerequisites

**Accounts Needed:**
1. ✅ GitHub (repository created)
2. ⏳ Vercel (for hosting)
3. ⏳ Supabase (for database)
4. ⏳ GoHighLevel Developer Account (for OAuth)
5. ⏳ Inngest (for workflows)

### Step 1: Environment Setup

**1. Create Supabase Project**
```bash
1. Go to https://supabase.com
2. Create new project
3. Run database migrations from /supabase/migrations/
4. Copy connection details
```

**2. Create Vercel Project**
```bash
1. Go to https://vercel.com
2. Import GitHub repository: natelasko528/ghl-onboarding-agent
3. Configure environment variables (see below)
4. Deploy
```

**3. Set Up GoHighLevel OAuth**
```bash
1. Go to GHL Marketplace Developer Portal
2. Create new OAuth app
3. Set redirect URI: https://your-domain.vercel.app/api/auth/ghl/callback
4. Copy Client ID and Client Secret
```

**4. Configure Inngest**
```bash
1. Go to https://inngest.com
2. Create new app
3. Copy Event Key and Signing Key
4. Set webhook URL: https://your-domain.vercel.app/api/inngest
```

### Step 2: Environment Variables

Create `.env.local` in project root:

```bash
# Application
NODE_ENV=production
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-domain.vercel.app

# Supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key

# GoHighLevel
GHL_CLIENT_ID=your_ghl_client_id
GHL_CLIENT_SECRET=your_ghl_client_secret
GHL_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-domain.vercel.app/api/auth/ghl/callback
NEXT_PUBLIC_GHL_APP_ID=your_ghl_app_id

# Inngest
INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=your_inngest_event_key
INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=your_inngest_signing_key
NEXT_PUBLIC_INNGEST_ENV=production

# JWT Secret (generate with: openssl rand -base64 32)
JWT_SECRET=your_random_32_char_secret

# Rate Limiting
RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=100
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000
```

### Step 3: Database Setup

```bash
# 1. Connect to Supabase
npx supabase link --project-ref your-project-ref

# 2. Run migrations
npx supabase db push

# 3. Generate TypeScript types
npm run db:generate-types

# 4. Seed test data (optional)
npx supabase db seed
```

### Step 4: Deploy to Vercel

**Option A: Automatic (Recommended)**
```bash
# Push to GitHub main branch
git add .
git commit -m "Initial deployment"
git push origin main

# Vercel will auto-deploy
```

**Option B: Manual**
```bash
# Install Vercel CLI
npm i -g vercel

# Deploy
vercel

# Set environment variables
vercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
vercel env add SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# ... (add all env vars)

# Deploy to production
vercel --prod
```

### Step 5: Post-Deployment Checklist

- [ ] Verify all environment variables are set
- [ ] Test database connection (`/api/health`)
- [ ] Test GHL OAuth flow (`/api/auth/ghl/authorize`)
- [ ] Create test user account
- [ ] Submit Stage 1 form test
- [ ] Check Supabase tables for data
- [ ] Review error logs in Vercel
- [ ] Set up monitoring alerts
- [ ] Configure custom domain (optional)

